%% LSEG Variance — the questions this approach answers (companion to the waterfall SVG)
%% v0.1 · conceptual · for validation · Viridian-proposed, not LSEG-ratified
%% NOTE: the horizontal variance bridge is a WATERFALL — Mermaid has no waterfall,
%% so LSEG_Variance_Storytelling_v0.1.svg remains the source of truth for the bars.
%% This companion captures only the "questions this answers" content, editable for Miro.
%% Fallback: change first line to "graph TD".
flowchart TD
  HUB["Variance storytelling — every bar drills to specific named deals.<br/>Horizontal bridge: opening forecast → takes (adds) minus puts (reduces) → closing forecast."]:::hub

  Q1["Why did the forecast move?"]:::q
  Q2["Did Commit actually commit?"]:::q
  Q3["Did the tail convert at the assumed rate?"]:::q
  Q4["Did new pipeline materialise as modelled?"]:::q
  Q5["Which deals slipped (absorbed vs incremental)?"]:::q
  Q6["How much of the forecast is deal-based vs overlay?"]:::q

  TAKE["Takes = new deals in, accelerated / upgraded"]:::take
  PUT["Puts = slipped, value-cut, lost"]:::put

  HUB --> Q1
  HUB --> Q2
  HUB --> Q3
  HUB --> Q4
  HUB --> Q5
  HUB --> Q6
  HUB -.- TAKE
  HUB -.- PUT

  classDef hub fill:#1F3864,stroke:#132444,color:#ffffff
  classDef q fill:#DCE6F5,stroke:#5E82BE,color:#1F3864
  classDef take fill:#3E9E6B,stroke:#2E8B57,color:#ffffff
  classDef put fill:#D06A57,stroke:#C0503C,color:#ffffff
